{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/110069-absorption-by-a-greater-titan","id":110069,"title":"Absorption by a Greater Titan?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-10T07:15:36-07:00","id":110069,"title":"Absorption by a Greater Titan?","content":"My players just made the transition into God. I have been refreshing myself after a year-long absence from the game on the mechanics of Overworlds and Titan Realms. On page 1 of Chapter 1 in God it talks about how a God in spirit form risks absorption by a Greater Titan while within it's realm. I thought I remembered seeing mechanics for this somewhere else in the book but I can't seem to find it.<br /> <br /> Can someone else please point me to a page number where I'm missing this?<br /> <br /> Or if I'm misremembering and the mechanics don't exist, has anyone else created a system to simulate this activity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2692-captain-morganism","name":"Captain Morganism","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2692_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T12:18:57-07:00","id":110209,"title":"","content":"I'm 70% there isn't a mechanic for this as it has been presented in god as more of a story event. Vaguely recall in the metaplot of the god book it mentions Gaia potentially suffering this fate if she were to use the world boddy to ruin the Greek's day. To my knowledge nobody has created anything for such an event either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/731-lurker","name":"Lurker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar731_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T15:38:02-07:00","id":110347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Morganism</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/110069-absorption-by-a-greater-titan#post110069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or if I'm misremembering and the mechanics don't exist, has anyone else created a system to simulate this activity?</div> </div> </div> </div>When I was running RAW, I would require the god in question to expend 1 Willpower per turn to resist being absorbed. When I moved away from RAW I required an (Intelligence <b>OR</b> Wits + Integrity + Willpower) roll with any result below a target difficulty resulting in conceptual damage.<br /> <br /> What actually happens after you have been absorbed by a Greater Titan would depend on the story in question, but it almost always involves that character no longer being playable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}